<Legal
  title="Preview Subprocessors"
  description="Convex, Cloudflare, WorkOS and Google Workspace provide the backend, storage, sign-in, hosting and email for Volli’s invite-only preview."
  path="/legal/subprocessors/"
>
  <p>
    These are the service providers Volli uses to process data for the invite-only 0.3
    preview. This is a preview list, not a list of planned integrations.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Convex, Inc.</strong> — backend database and server functions. Processes
      account, Workspace, membership, board, configuration and Session records,
      credentials you choose to store, connected-account and repository metadata, and
      device and runner metadata needed for the service.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> — website and docs hosting, and object storage for
      synced Session transcript bodies, agent logs, attachments and move-staging uploads.
      Processes uploaded content and connection information for requests to its services.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>WorkOS, Inc.</strong> — AuthKit sign-in and authentication sessions. Processes
      profile and identity information, email, and sign-in connection and session metadata.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Workspace (Google)</strong> — email for support, privacy, security and
      legal correspondence. Processes sender and recipient details, messages, attachments
      you send us and our replies. It does not receive your Workspace history merely
      because you sign in.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers may process data outside Canada, including in the United States and
    on global networks. We make no region-specific storage promise for this preview.
  </p>
  <h2>Services you choose</h2>
  <p>
    Model providers, gateways, git hosts, MCP servers and other tools you connect are
    services you direct, not additional Volli preview subprocessors. They can receive
    prompts, code or other data you send, under your agreements with them. Your own machine
    runs the preview's agent tools and calls the model provider or gateway you choose;
    the preview does not use a Volli-operated model relay. GitHub also receives connection
    information when our download page requests release information in your browser,
    or the app checks for and downloads updates from GitHub Releases. Google or GitHub
    also handles your sign-in identity when you choose it through WorkOS AuthKit, under
    that identity provider's own terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will update this list before adding a provider that processes preview data.
    Questions or privacy requests can be sent to
    <a href="mailto:privacy@volli.app">privacy@volli.app</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
